  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n`stakingLimit` is responsible for limiting the total staked amount in the system, which is a well known mechanism. The issue is that, performed calculations in `stakingLimit`, overestimate the total `netStaked` `HYPE` in the protocol, because it does not consider `totalSlashing`.\n\n```solidity\nfunction stake() public payable nonReentrant whenNotPaused whenStakingNotPaused {\n\n        ...\n\n        if (stakingLimit > 0) {\n            // Get rewards from ValidatorManager to account for earned rewards\n            // This approach uses global rewards but provides a reasonable approximation\n            // for this StakingManager's available capacity\n            uint256 rewardsAmount = validatorManager.totalRewards();\n            uint256 netStaked = totalStaked + rewardsAmount - totalClaimed;\n            require(netStaked + msg.value <= stakingLimit, \"Staking limit reached\");\n        }\n\n        ... \n\n    }\n```\n\nWe can see that `netStaked` is calculated as `(totalStaked + rewardsAmount - totalClaimed)`.\n\n- `totalStaked` represents total amount ever staked in the protocol\n- `totalClaimed` represents total amount ever claimed from the protocol\n- `rewardsAmount` represents total amount of rewards ever earned in the protocol\n\nThere is no `slashedAmount` which represents total amount ever slashed in the protocol. Total slashing affects staking limit because it \"removes\" `HYPE` from the protocol making space for new deposits. However it is not included in the calculations, which leads to overestimation of the `netStaked`, which can prevent new deposits. New deposits allow earning new rewards, which is essential for the protocol, that's why the `stakingLimit` check is very important.\n\nAssume that `stakingLimit` is 500:\n\n- totalStaked is 400\n- totalClaimed is 100\n- totalRewards is 200\n\nNow the stakingLimit is achieved, because `400 + 200 - 100 = 500`\n\nIf we consider that totalSlashed is 50 the `stakingLimit` shows that there is no space for new deposits, however the `REAL` HYPE amount in the protocol is equal to `450`, which allows depositing additional `50` HYPE.\n\n`netStaked` is incorrectly calculated in the `stake` function, overestimating the real total `HYPE` amount in the system, preventing potential new deposits.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nSubtract total slashed amount from `netStaked` to correctly calculate the real `HYPE` amount in the protocol and allow for new depoits.\n\n```diff\nfunction stake() public payable nonReentrant whenNotPaused whenStakingNotPaused {\n        // Check whitelist if enabled\n        if (whitelistEnabled) {\n            require(isWhitelisted(msg.sender), \"Address not whitelisted\");\n        }\n\n        // Validate stake amount\n        require(msg.value >= minStakeAmount, \"Stake amount below minimum\");\n        if (maxStakeAmount > 0) {\n            require(msg.value <= maxStakeAmount, \"Stake amount above maximum\");\n        }\n        if (stakingLimit > 0) {\n            // Get rewards from ValidatorManager to account for earned rewards\n            // This approach uses global rewards but provides a reasonable approximation\n            // for this StakingManager's available capacity\n            uint256 rewardsAmount = validatorManager.totalRewards();\n+           uint256 slashedAmount = validatorManager.totalSlashing();\n+           uint256 netStaked = totalStaked + rewardsAmount - totalClaimed - slashedAmount;\n-           uint256 netStaked = totalStaked + rewardsAmount - totalClaimed;\n            require(netStaked + msg.value <= stakingLimit, \"Staking limit reached\");\n        }\n\n        totalStaked += msg.value;\n\n        // Convert HYPE to kHYPE amount using exchange ratio\n        uint256 kHYPEAmount = stakingAccountant.HYPEToKHYPE(msg.value);\n\n        // Mint kHYPE tokens based on the conversion\n        kHYPE.mint(msg.sender, kHYPEAmount);\n\n        _distributeStake(msg.value, OperationType.UserDeposit);\n\n        stakingAccountant.recordStake(msg.value);\n\n        emit StakeReceived(address(this), msg.sender, msg.value);\n    }\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "Please add this test to `test/StakingManager.t.sol` and run `forge test --mt \"test_stakingLimit\" -vvvv`.\n\n```solidity\nfunction test_stakingLimit() public {\n        vm.startPrank(manager);\n        stakingManager.setUnstakeFeeRate(0);\n        stakingManager.setTargetBuffer(0);\n        stakingManager.setStakingLimit(2e18);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        uint256 stakeAmount = 1 ether;\n        uint256 slashedAmount = stakeAmount / 2;\n\n        vm.startPrank(manager);\n        validatorManager.activateValidator(validator);\n        validatorManager.setDelegation(address(stakingManager), validator);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.deal(user, 2 * stakeAmount);\n        vm.prank(user);\n        stakingManager.stake{value: stakeAmount}();\n\n        vm.prank(user);\n        stakingManager.stake{value: stakeAmount}();\n\n        // Slash the validator\n        vm.prank(address(oracleManager));\n        validatorManager.updateValidatorPerformance(\n            validator,\n            stakeAmount,\n            8000,\n            7500,\n            9000,\n            8500\n        );\n\n        vm.prank(address(oracleManager));\n        validatorManager.reportSlashingEvent(validator, slashedAmount);\n\n        // User can't deposit\n        vm.deal(user, slashedAmount);\n        vm.prank(user);\n        vm.expectRevert(\"Staking limit reached\");\n        stakingManager.stake{value: slashedAmount}();\n    }\n```",
